  "reconciliation_audit": {
    "explanation": "Pooled metrics aggregate all 7,843 out-of-fold predictions into a single global confusion matrix, weighting every farm equally. In contrast, fold-mean metrics calculate Macro-F1 independently on each validation fold partition (N ~ 1,508 to 1,610) and then take the unweighted arithmetic mean. Because minority crop sample counts (e.g., Red Gram N=221, Chillies N=601) vary across spatial folds, per-fold class F1 denominators fluctuate slightly, leading to slight divergence between pooled and mean-fold F1. Both metrics are valid, with pooled Macro-F1 providing the unbiased population estimate across the full cohort.",
